  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 DRA Storm Freddy Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This DRA-funded Acute Crisis Joint Response, targets communities affected by Tropical Cyclone Freddy, which hit Mozambique in March 2023. Response partners will ensure a multi-sectorial response with focus on WASH, Food Security and Livelihoods, education, protection, and shelter. The programme sector specific interventions integrate protection mainstreaming to maximize impact for the targeted individuals, households and communities affected by TC Freddy. Proposed interventions are aligned with SPHERE standards, sector specific standards, and in line with local sector working group agreements in country. SOS NL partners with SOS Mozambique and local NGO Livaningo to implement WASH and Protection activities in Mopeia district (Zambezia Province) and Caia district (Sofala province).</narrative>
  </description>
